# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Timer-driven oneshot units that write via systemd `StandardOutput=append:`.
#
# Every log below was covered by NO logrotate stanza until 2026-09-01.
# flyer-recovery-watchdog.log had reached 105 MB and was still growing; the
# rest were small only because their units run rarely, which is luck rather
# than design. tests/test_logrotate_coverage.py now fails if a unit gains an
# append: target without a stanza here.
#
# `create`, not copytruncate: all of these are Type=oneshot fired by a timer,
# so the process exits between runs and holds no fd across the rotation
# window. An earlier draft used copytruncate on the theory that `append:`
# implies a long-lived fd; the coverage test disproved it by failing on
# send-daily-brief, eod-reconcile and prune-expense-receipts, which are the
# same shape and have always used `create`.
#
# 0640 shift-agent shift-agent matches the stanzas above and the units'
# `User=`. On-disk ownership today is inconsistent (some root:root from
# systemd having created the file first); rotation normalises it. systemd
# reopens the path each run, so the change is invisible to the units.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

